# Admin-Risk Register — v2 PROPOSAL (2026-04-20)
# Operator review required before this replaces v1.
#
# Expansion scope: v1 (17 entries) → v2 (~40 entries) capturing landscape shift post
# EO 14151 (Ending Radical and Wasteful Government DEI Programs, 2025-01-20) and
# EO 14168 (Defending Women from Gender Ideology Extremism, 2025-01-20).
#
# Severity tiers (unchanged from v1):
#   RED     = documented pull / funding denied / program terminated
#   YELLOW  = agency memo, leaked list, or algorithmic scrutiny trigger (not confirmed denial)
#   GREEN   = precautionary; sector-dependent (progressive / soul-fire register may welcome)
#
# Law 4 discipline: Logician flags, NEVER rewrites. Applicant approves EVERY substitution.
# Context matters: "gender" in biological/clinical context ≠ "gender" as DEI framing;
# "women" in WOSB/SBA programs ≠ "women" as DEI identity category. Use context field per entry.
#
# Sources driving v2 additions:
#   - EO 14151 "Ending Radical and Wasteful Government DEI Programs and Preferencing" (2025-01-20)
#   - EO 14168 "Defending Women from Gender Ideology Extremism" (2025-01-20)
#   - NSF leaked ~108-keyword flagging list (2025-02; multiple press confirmations)
#   - NIH computational-text-analysis scanning (no public list, but staff directive confirmed)
#   - NEA 2026 funding conditions (no "gender ideology" promotion)
#   - "Big Beautiful Bill" prohibition on federal funding for gender-affirming care
#   - 360+ federal surveys removing sexual orientation / gender identity measures (Williams Institute)
#   - Jan 2026 partial reversal on NIH DEI criteria for stalled health research grants (Trump admin dropped criteria)

version: 2.2
supersedes: admin_risk_register.yaml (v1, 17 entries)
date: 2026-04-20
operator_review: PENDING
operator_approval_token: null

# =====================================================================
# TWO-AXIS DIALECT DISCIPLINE (per Law 4 / CLAUDE.md)
# =====================================================================
#
# The `severity` field on each entry is the FEDERAL admin-risk tier only.
# The same term may be neutral, expected, or PREFERRED in progressive /
# racial-justice / community-foundation dialects — especially for
# applicants who are Black-led, Latino-led, tribal-led, LGBTQ+-led, or
# otherwise identity-rooted organizations applying to funders that
# explicitly center those identities.
#
# The register is NOT a prohibition list. It is a dialect-aware flagging
# system. Applicant approves every substitution.
#
# Each entry carries (in addition to federal severity) a `progressive_register`
# field with these values:
#
#   AVOID     — even progressive funders avoid (e.g., reclaimed pejoratives)
#   OK        — usable but not expected; no signal either way
#   EXPECTED  — progressive / racial-justice funders expect to see this language;
#               its absence may signal misalignment
#   PREFERRED — progressive / racial-justice / community-foundation funders
#               actively welcome and amplify this language; using it
#               signals alignment with the funder's stated values
#
# Funder-register categories (based on Josh's four-category taxonomy per CLAUDE.md):
#
#   federal / federal-contract                    → severity tier governs
#   state (conservative)                          → maps to federal severity, often softer
#   state (progressive — CA, WA, OR, NY, IL, MA)  → maps to progressive_register, often EXPECTED
#   foundation (conservative/traditionalist)      → maps to federal severity, often softer
#   foundation (centrist — Rockefeller, Gates)    → context-mixed; OK for most; avoid RED-tier
#   foundation (progressive — Ford, MacArthur,
#               Kellogg, Heinz, Surdna, Nathan
#               Cummings, Packard on env)         → progressive_register governs; often EXPECTED
#   foundation (racial-justice — Kellogg racial-
#               equity programs, Surdna, Libra,
#               Borealis, NEO Philanthropy,
#               Hispanics in Philanthropy,
#               ABFE, Kresge)                     → progressive_register = PREFERRED for
#                                                    identity-affirming language when
#                                                    applicant is identity-rooted
#   foundation (soul-fire — radical, activist,
#               abolitionist-aligned: Borealis,
#               Groundswell, Resist, Third Wave,
#               Brainerd)                         → progressive_register governs; many GREEN-tier
#                                                    terms are PREFERRED; reclaimed language welcome
#
# Applicant-identity overlay:
#
#   When the applicant organization is Black-led, Latino-led, tribal-led,
#   immigrant-serving, LGBTQ+-led, or otherwise identity-rooted, AND the
#   funder is in the progressive / racial-justice / soul-fire registers,
#   the flagged terms that name the applicant's own identity or lived
#   reality are typically EXPECTED to PREFERRED — code-switching AWAY
#   from identity-affirming language in that context can itself signal
#   misalignment with the funder.
#
# Default mapping when `progressive_register` is not explicitly set:
#
#   federal RED + DEI/identity framing  → progressive EXPECTED
#   federal RED + gender-framing        → progressive OK (some progressive
#                                          funders still code-switching
#                                          cautiously post-EO 14168)
#   federal RED + climate/ESG framing   → progressive EXPECTED (climate funders
#                                          explicitly welcome the language the
#                                          federal admin rejects)
#   federal YELLOW + identity framing   → progressive OK to EXPECTED
#   federal GREEN + activist framing    → progressive EXPECTED to PREFERRED
#
# =====================================================================

expansion_cycles:
  - v2 (2026-04-20): 17 → 40 entries. Added trans/LGBTQ+/gender family (RED), NSF leaked 108-keyword coverage (YELLOW), context-dependent caveats (women/female/disabilities/minority/underserved).
  - v2.1 (2026-04-20): 40 → ~75 entries. Added ESG/climate/green axis (RED: climate change, green, ESG, renewable energy, clean energy, carbon, net-zero, decarbonization, greenhouse gas, just transition); health axis (RED: health equity, structural racism, SDOH); reproductive axis (RED: reproductive rights/justice, abortion); analytical-DEI vocabulary expansion (YELLOW: community-centered, culturally responsive, lived experience, amplify, center, representation, allyship, safe space, microaggressions, positionality, white privilege/supremacy, cisgender, patriarchy); immigration axis (YELLOW: DACA, undocumented, sanctuary, asylum); clinical-DEI axis (YELLOW: trauma-informed, SEL, harm reduction); additional climate YELLOW (sustainability, climate resilience, global warming, impact investing, stakeholder capitalism, triple bottom line).
  - v2.2 (2026-04-20): added two-axis dialect discipline. `progressive_register` field added to high-divergence entries. Schema preserves single-axis v2.1 data for terms where federal + progressive agree; explicit field populated for terms where they diverge (the common case for identity-rooted applicants to progressive funders). Default-mapping rules documented in top block. This update is taxonomic, not content — zero entries removed, most severity tiers unchanged.
verification_discipline: |
  Each entry's `documented_action` field cites the evidence class (EO / agency memo / leaked list /
  press confirmation / Court filing). RED tier requires documented pull or denial. YELLOW tier can
  rest on leaked list or agency-memo scrutiny. GREEN tier is precautionary without documented
  enforcement action. Operator may downgrade or remove any entry — applicant sovereignty over
  flagged-term register is absolute (Law 5).

entries:

  # =====================================================================
  # RED tier — documented funding pulls, denials, or program terminations
  # =====================================================================

  - term: "DEI"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # progressive/racial-justice funders expect this language; identity-rooted applicants should use without substitution
    context: "Executive Order 14151 directly targets DEI programs in federal grants"
    documented_action: "EO 14151 (2025-01-20) directs termination of DEI activities across federal government + DEI-related grant criteria; multiple agencies have implemented"
    alternatives: ["workforce development", "broad participation", "inclusive access", "community representation"]
    notes: "Acronym and spelled-out form both flagged"
    variants: ["diversity equity inclusion", "diversity, equity, and inclusion", "D.E.I.", "DEIA", "diversity equity inclusion accessibility"]

  - term: "equity"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # progressive funders expect; racial-justice funders PREFERRED for Black/Latino-led applicants
    context: "When used as standalone social-policy term in federal applications"
    documented_action: "Federal grant reviewers instructed to flag equity-focused framing; NSF leaked list includes equity"
    alternatives: ["access", "opportunity", "fairness", "broad participation"]
    notes: "Context-dependent — 'equity' in financial context (owner's equity, home equity) is fine. Flag only when used as social/policy framing."
    variants: ["equitable", "inequity", "inequitable"]

  - term: "environmental justice"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # climate/environmental-justice-aligned foundations PREFERRED; EJ-focused funders expect the exact phrase
    context: "Term flagged in EPA and DOE grant programs under current administration"
    documented_action: "EPA Environmental Justice programs restructured 2025; term discouraged in federal applications"
    alternatives: ["environmental protection", "community environmental health", "pollution reduction", "clean air and water access"]
    variants: ["EJ", "environmental equity"]

  - term: "climate justice"
    severity: RED
    context: "Flagged alongside environmental justice"
    documented_action: "Term removed from multiple federal program descriptions 2025"
    alternatives: ["climate resilience", "weather preparedness", "agricultural adaptation", "resource conservation"]
    variants: ["climate equity"]

  - term: "transgender"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: OK  # LGBTQ-focused funders EXPECTED; general progressive register softer (some foundations code-switching cautiously in 2026 post-EO 14168)
    context: "EO 14168 directs replacement of gender with sex; NIH grants terminated on trans-health research; HIV services denied for trans individuals"
    documented_action: "EO 14168 (2025-01-20); NIH grant terminations for LGBTQ health research (documented by ASCO, KFF); HHS directives"
    alternatives: ["use biological terminology if clinically relevant", "community members", "patients", "individuals"]
    notes: "RED in any federal application. Context-sensitive reclamation in progressive foundation applications (dialect code-switch); risky in government-adjacent funding."
    variants: ["trans", "transgendered", "trans*", "transsexual"]

  - term: "LGBTQ"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # LGBTQ-focused foundations (Astraea, Arcus, Ford's Sexuality & Gender Justice) PREFERRED; non-LGBTQ progressive funders EXPECTED
    context: "Federal surveys removed 360+ SOGI measures since 2025-01-20; grant programs terminated"
    documented_action: "Williams Institute tracked 360+ federal data-collection removals; NSF leaked list includes LGBT; NIH scanning; NEA 2026 'no gender ideology promotion' clause"
    alternatives: ["community", "the community we serve", "diverse populations (where clinically relevant, use specific clinical terms)"]
    variants: ["LGBTQ+", "LGBTQIA+", "LGBTQI", "LGBT", "queer", "GLBT"]

  - term: "gender identity"
    severity: RED
    context: "EO 14168 directs federal agencies to recognize only male/female biological sex; 'gender identity' framing triggers scrutiny"
    documented_action: "EO 14168 (2025-01-20); Williams Institute survey-removal tracking; multiple agency directives"
    alternatives: ["biological sex (where applicable)", "patient identity (clinical)", "personal characteristics"]
    variants: ["gender expression", "gender nonconforming", "nonbinary", "non-binary"]

  - term: "gender-affirming"
    severity: RED
    context: "Federal funding explicitly prohibited by 2025 legislation"
    documented_action: "Big Beautiful Bill prohibits federal funding for gender-affirming care; HHS directives; documented revocations"
    alternatives: ["consult the specific RFA — if the program supports clinical care, use the program's own terminology"]
    variants: ["gender affirming", "gender-affirmation", "transition-related"]

  - term: "gender ideology"
    severity: RED
    context: "EO 14168 title explicitly rejects 'gender ideology'; NEA 2026 requires projects not promote it"
    documented_action: "EO 14168; NEA 2026 compliance requirements"
    alternatives: ["avoid the term entirely; do not use ironically or critically in federal applications"]
    notes: "Even critical or academic use triggers scrutiny. Rhetorical cost exceeds analytical benefit in federal filings."

  - term: "sexual orientation"
    severity: RED
    context: "Williams Institute tracked removal of SOGI questions from 360+ federal surveys post-2025-01-20"
    documented_action: "Executive action cascade; agency survey modifications"
    alternatives: ["community members", "patients (clinical)", "populations served"]
    variants: ["SOGI", "LGB"]

  - term: "underrepresented"
    severity: RED
    context: "NSF leaked keyword list flagged; widely reported research-grant omissions"
    documented_action: "NSF 108-keyword flagging list (leaked 2025-02); multiple researcher reports of proposals omitting the term"
    alternatives: ["historically excluded from (specific program)", "first-generation", "below-parity representation", "communities with lower historical participation rates"]
    variants: ["underrepresentation", "underrepresented minority", "URM"]

  - term: "women"
    severity: RED
    context: "NSF leaked list includes 'women' and 'female' as flagged; context-dependent — WOSB/SBA women-owned-business programs still valid and required to use the term"
    documented_action: "NSF leaked 108-keyword list; reported omissions from research grants"
    alternatives: ["context matters — in WOSB programs, 'women-owned small business' is the required federal term; in research framing, avoid 'women' as identity category"]
    notes: "Hardest-to-advise entry. WOSB certification programs explicitly require the term. NSF/NIH research proposals should avoid. Applicant approves per-document."
    variants: ["women's", "womens", "female", "female-led", "female-focused", "women-led"]

  - term: "minority"
    severity: RED
    context: "NSF leaked list; Trump admin explicit anti-DEI stance"
    documented_action: "NSF flagged-list press confirmations; agency DEI-removal directives"
    alternatives: ["historically limited-access populations", "communities with lower participation rates", "specific demographic term if legally relevant (e.g., SDA per USDA definition)"]
    notes: "USDA SDA (Socially Disadvantaged Applicant) definition is statutory and remains valid — use 'SDA' not 'minority'."
    variants: ["minorities", "minority-owned", "minority-serving", "underrepresented minority", "URM"]

  # =====================================================================
  # YELLOW tier — agency memos / leaked lists / scrutiny triggers
  # =====================================================================

  - term: "systemic racism"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Agency memos cautioning against framing in grant narratives"
    alternatives: ["historical patterns", "structural barriers", "documented disparities", "historical access gaps"]
    variants: ["systemic inequity", "structural racism", "systemic oppression"]

  - term: "social justice"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # progressive/racial-justice/soul-fire funders PREFERRED; abolitionist funders welcome explicitly
    context: "Cautioned in federal applications; less risky in progressive foundations"
    alternatives: ["community wellbeing", "fair treatment", "equal opportunity (carefully — itself flagged)"]
    notes: "Foundation grants (progressive register) may welcome this term — check dialect per Law 4"

  - term: "transformative justice"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Cautioned in federal applications"
    alternatives: ["restorative approaches", "community-based solutions", "alternative resolution"]

  - term: "BIPOC"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: PREFERRED  # racial-justice funders (ABFE, Hispanics in Philanthropy, NCG member foundations) PREFERRED; Black/Latino-led applicants to racial-justice funders should NOT code-switch away
    context: "Some federal reviewers flagged as political terminology; NSF flagged list"
    alternatives: ["underserved communities (itself flagged — see below)", "historically underrepresented groups (also flagged)", "specific statutory terms (e.g., SDA for USDA)"]
    notes: "Acceptable in progressive/soul-fire foundations. In federal applications, prefer statutory terms (SDA, Beginning Farmer, Veteran-Owned, etc.) over demographic labels."

  - term: "anti-racism"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Cautioned in federal applications post-2025 executive orders"
    alternatives: ["inclusive practices (also flagged — see below)", "bias reduction", "fair treatment protocols"]
    variants: ["antiracist", "anti-racist"]

  - term: "decolonize"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Cautioned in federal and some state applications"
    alternatives: ["community self-determination", "locally-led", "culturally grounded"]
    variants: ["decolonization", "decolonizing"]

  - term: "reparations"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Highly charged in any government-adjacent funding"
    alternatives: ["community investment", "restorative funding", "targeted support"]
    variants: ["reparative"]

  - term: "marginalized"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # progressive/racial-justice funders expect; some soul-fire funders prefer self-determination framing
    context: "NSF leaked keyword list; widely documented researcher self-censorship"
    alternatives: ["historically excluded", "populations with lower participation rates", "specific statutory demographic (e.g., SDA)"]
    variants: ["marginalize", "marginalization"]

  - term: "diversity"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list; DEI context flagged (biological diversity, crop diversity, species diversity — SAFE)"
    alternatives: ["broad participation", "variety of (species / crops / approaches)", "range of perspectives"]
    notes: "Clinical / ecological / scientific 'diversity' (biodiversity, crop diversity) is unflagged. Social 'diversity' as DEI framing is flagged."
    variants: ["diverse", "diversify"]

  - term: "inclusion"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "When used as DEI framing; 'financial inclusion' and similar sector-specific uses are safer"
    alternatives: ["broad participation", "open access", "wide enrollment"]
    variants: ["inclusive", "inclusivity"]

  - term: "critical race theory"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Politicized term; avoid in federal applications"
    alternatives: ["do not use; reframe without analytical framework citation"]
    variants: ["CRT"]

  - term: "woke"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: AVOID  # reclaimed status contested; even progressive/soul-fire funders avoid due to pejorative-conservative-discourse capture
    context: "Politicized pejorative in federal-administration discourse; ironic use risky"
    alternatives: ["do not use in federal applications"]
    variants: ["wokeness", "woke ideology"]

  - term: "disparities"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Flagged when paired with identity categories (racial disparities, gender disparities); clinical disparities (health outcomes) more context-tolerant"
    alternatives: ["documented differences in outcomes", "gaps in access to", "measured variation across"]
    notes: "Clinical 'health disparities' is in gray zone — may be acceptable in CDC / HHS clinical framing depending on administration guidance week-to-week."

  - term: "sense of belonging"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list"
    alternatives: ["community engagement", "program retention", "participant connection"]

  - term: "institutional"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list; primarily flagged in 'institutional racism' / 'institutional bias' framing, not in 'institutional capacity' or 'institutional partner'"
    alternatives: ["context matters — 'institutional capacity' in org-development is fine; 'institutional racism/bias' framing is flagged"]
    notes: "Single-word flagging depends heavily on context. Applicant reviews per-use."

  - term: "activism"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list"
    alternatives: ["community engagement", "civic participation", "advocacy (itself sometimes flagged — check program)"]
    variants: ["activist", "activists"]

  - term: "prejudice"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list"
    alternatives: ["bias", "disparities in treatment", "documented discrimination"]

  - term: "privilege"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "As analytical frame in DEI discourse; 'attorney-client privilege' or similar legal/technical uses are unflagged"
    alternatives: ["historical advantage", "structural access (itself flagged)", "varying starting conditions"]
    notes: "Context matters — legal 'privilege' (attorney-client) is fine; sociological 'privilege' as DEI analysis is flagged."
    variants: ["privileged"]

  - term: "disabilities"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list included; ADA-statutory use (Americans with Disabilities Act, disability services) remains valid"
    alternatives: ["context matters — ADA/Section 504 programs require the term; DEI-framed research proposals should be careful"]
    notes: "This is the canonical example of context-dependent flagging. The statutory term 'disability' in ADA programs is valid and required. 'Disability' as DEI identity category is flagged."
    variants: ["disability", "disabled", "people with disabilities"]

  - term: "underserved"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # community foundations + health/education funders expect; USDA statutory 'underserved producer' remains valid at federal level
    context: "Widely flagged in federal applications; USDA statutory 'underserved producer' definition remains valid"
    alternatives: ["context matters — USDA 'underserved producer' is statutory and valid; DEI-framed use is flagged"]
    notes: "Similar to 'minority' — USDA statutory definitions preserve valid uses; general DEI-framed use is flagged."
    variants: ["under-served"]

  - term: "female"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list; biological/clinical 'female' (sex variable in research) more tolerant than 'female-led' or 'female-owned' as identity"
    alternatives: ["context matters — clinical sex-as-variable is valid; 'female-led' organization framing is flagged"]
    notes: "Crossover with 'women' entry. WOSB programs require 'women-owned' terminology."
    variants: ["females"]

  - term: "equal opportunity"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "NSF leaked list; statutory 'Equal Opportunity Employer' compliance statements remain valid"
    alternatives: ["open enrollment", "accessible to all eligible applicants", "statutory EOE language where legally required"]
    notes: "EOE compliance boilerplate is required by federal contractors and unaffected. 'Equal opportunity' as policy framing is flagged."

  # =====================================================================
  # GREEN tier — precautionary / sector-dependent / progressive-register-safe
  # =====================================================================

  - term: "food sovereignty"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Progressive food-systems framing; risky in federal; welcomed in Shared Capital, La Vía Campesina-adjacent foundations"
    alternatives: ["food security (federal-safe)", "local food systems", "community-controlled food production"]

  - term: "land back"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Indigenous land-return framing; high rhetorical cost in federal applications"
    alternatives: ["tribal land stewardship", "indigenous-led conservation", "First Nations partnership"]
    variants: ["#LandBack"]

  - term: "solidarity economy"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Cooperative economics framing; welcomed in Seed Commons / New Economy Coalition foundations"
    alternatives: ["cooperative economy", "community-owned enterprises", "shared-ownership economic models"]

  - term: "mutual aid"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Cross-partisan in emergency response; politicized in some contexts"
    alternatives: ["community response", "peer support networks", "community-based emergency assistance"]

  - term: "abolition"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Prison-abolition framing; high rhetorical cost in federal applications; welcomed in progressive justice funders"
    alternatives: ["criminal legal reform", "community-based alternatives", "decarceration (also politicized)"]
    variants: ["abolitionist"]

  - term: "intersectional"
    severity: GREEN
    context: "Academic-origin DEI analytical frame; v1 had this in GREEN, v2 keeps — landscape has shifted but 'intersectional' has not been singled out at the level of 'DEI' or 'underrepresented'"
    alternatives: ["multi-factor analysis", "considering multiple dimensions", "compound circumstances"]
    notes: "Operator may move to YELLOW at discretion. Kept GREEN pending documented federal pull."
    variants: ["intersectionality"]

  # =====================================================================
  # v2.1 EXPANSION (2026-04-20) — ESG / climate / health / reproductive / immigration axes
  # =====================================================================
  # Operator flag: "not sure if the list is comprehensive enough to cover all the DEI ESG
  # Green words this admin scans bans and generally doesn't approve of" — confirmed accurate.
  # Sources (see v2.1 sources block below): Inside Climate News ($29B climate/env grants
  # canceled or frozen); DOE banned-words reporting (NPR Sept 2025); NIH health-equity /
  # structural-racism pause (Notus); EPA/DOE/USDA REAP cancellations; court injunctions on
  # $14B green-bank grants + $20B EPA program (show some pushback, but the scanning persists).
  #
  # =====================================================================

  # ---- RED additions (climate / ESG — documented grant terminations) ----

  - term: "climate change"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # climate funders (Hewlett, Packard, Energy Foundation, ClimateWorks) PREFERRED; code-switching AWAY would signal misalignment
    context: "DOE directed to avoid the phrase in grant materials (NPR Sept 2025); $29B in climate/environment grants canceled or frozen 2025"
    documented_action: "DOE banned-words directive; EPA green-bank $20B termination (partially blocked by court); broad grant freezes under EO 14008 rescission"
    alternatives: ["weather variability", "long-term weather patterns", "extreme weather preparedness", "resource conservation"]
    variants: ["climate crisis", "climate emergency"]

  - term: "green"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # progressive environmental/climate/green-economy funders PREFERRED; economic-justice funders welcome 'green jobs' explicitly
    context: "Flagged in federal program framing (DOE directive per NPR); 'green jobs', 'green economy', 'green infrastructure' all scrutinized; ecological 'green' in specific contexts may survive (e.g., NRCS cover-crop programs)"
    documented_action: "DOE banned-words list (Sept 2025); $29B in green-labeled grants canceled or frozen"
    alternatives: ["context-dependent — 'conservation infrastructure', 'resource-efficient', 'low-input' often work; in ag contexts, cite the statutory program (EQIP, CSP, RCPP)"]
    notes: "Ecological 'green' (photosynthesis, vegetation) is fine. Policy 'green' (green jobs, green economy, green new deal) is RED."
    variants: ["green jobs", "green economy", "green infrastructure", "green new deal"]

  - term: "ESG"
    severity: RED
    context: "EO explicitly targets 'environmental, social, and governance (ESG)' state laws and initiatives"
    documented_action: "EO targeting state ESG laws (April 2025 Holland & Knight summary); SEC rollback of ESG disclosure rules; broad agency directives"
    alternatives: ["governance and risk management", "corporate responsibility (also risky)", "fiduciary compliance"]
    variants: ["environmental social governance", "environmental, social, and governance"]

  - term: "renewable energy"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # climate/energy-transition funders PREFERRED; state agencies in CA/WA/OR/NY still use openly
    context: "DOE canceled $7.5B in renewable energy grants across 315 awards (Oct 2025); USDA REAP rescinded (April 2026, NOFO FY25-27 eliminated)"
    documented_action: "DOE Oct 2025 termination (315 awards, $7.56B); USDA REAP rescission April 2026; legal challenges pending"
    alternatives: ["on-farm energy (USDA context)", "distributed generation", "energy independence", "rural energy (USDA context-specific)"]
    notes: "USDA REAP itself is rescinded; do not apply to a non-existent program. Other programs (EQIP energy-related practices) may still fund similar work without the 'renewable' framing."
    variants: ["renewables", "renewable power"]

  - term: "clean energy"
    severity: RED
    context: "DOE canceled $8B in clean-energy grants (Oct 2025); blue-state projects specifically targeted"
    documented_action: "DOE Oct 2025 termination announcements; PBS NewsHour coverage"
    alternatives: ["energy independence", "domestic energy production", "affordable energy", "on-farm energy (USDA context)"]
    variants: ["clean-energy", "clean power"]

  - term: "carbon"
    severity: RED
    context: "Policy framing ('carbon-neutral', 'net-zero carbon', 'carbon offset', 'carbon tax') flagged; scientific carbon (carbon-14 dating, carbon chemistry) unflagged"
    documented_action: "DOE banned-words directive; carbon-tax and GHG emissions grants targeted per EO"
    alternatives: ["context matters — scientific carbon is fine; policy carbon framing (neutrality, offsets, pricing) is flagged"]
    notes: "'Carbon sequestration' in soil-health contexts is borderline — USDA NRCS has funded it for decades as soil-carbon, but the political frame is risky. Use 'soil health' or 'soil organic matter' instead where possible."
    variants: ["carbon-neutral", "carbon neutral", "carbon-negative", "carbon offset", "carbon pricing", "carbon tax"]

  - term: "net-zero"
    severity: RED
    context: "Policy framing associated with Paris Accord / Green New Deal / climate-action targets"
    documented_action: "Cancellation of $500M Lebec Net-Zero cement project (May 2025); broad pattern of net-zero-labeled grant terminations"
    alternatives: ["energy-balanced", "self-sufficient operations", "cost-neutral operations"]
    variants: ["net zero", "net-zero emissions", "NZE"]

  - term: "decarbonization"
    severity: RED
    context: "Policy framing explicitly targeted"
    documented_action: "EO targeting state climate programs (April 2025); DOE terminology directives"
    alternatives: ["energy efficiency", "fuel diversification", "emissions reduction (also risky)"]
    variants: ["decarbonize", "decarbonise"]

  - term: "greenhouse gas"
    severity: RED
    context: "EO explicitly targets 'greenhouse gas' emissions programs"
    documented_action: "EO targeting state GHG programs; EPA methane rule rollback"
    alternatives: ["air emissions (broader)", "point-source emissions (regulatory context)"]
    variants: ["GHG", "greenhouse-gas", "GHGs"]

  - term: "environmental justice"
    severity: RED
    context: "ALREADY IN v2 — cross-referencing for completeness"
    documented_action: "See v2 entry above"
    alternatives: ["See v2 entry"]
    notes: "Retained from v2; not double-added."

  - term: "just transition"
    severity: RED
    context: "Labor + climate combined framing; politically charged"
    documented_action: "Associated with Green New Deal framing; grants using the phrase canceled in blue-state cancellations wave"
    alternatives: ["workforce adaptation", "sector diversification", "rural workforce development"]
    variants: ["just-transition"]

  # ---- RED additions (health — NIH explicitly paused) ----

  - term: "health equity"
    severity: RED
    progressive_register: EXPECTED  # health-focused foundations (RWJF, Commonwealth Fund, CHCF) PREFERRED; term absence signals non-alignment
    context: "NIH paused new funding for grants containing this term pending computational-text-analysis review (2025 guidance)"
    documented_action: "NIH directive to staff; Notus reporting; CDC page framing modified"
    alternatives: ["health outcomes", "access to care", "healthcare access across populations (without equity framing)"]
    variants: ["health-equity", "equitable health", "health inequity"]

  - term: "structural racism"
    severity: RED
    context: "NIH paused new funding for grants containing this term pending review"
    documented_action: "NIH directive; Notus reporting"
    alternatives: ["historical disparities in outcomes", "documented access gaps", "systemic barriers (also flagged — see YELLOW 'systemic')"]
    variants: ["institutional racism", "systemic racism (already flagged)"]

  - term: "social determinants of health"
    severity: RED
    context: "NIH scanning-tool targets; CDC SDOH page modified post-2025"
    documented_action: "NIH computational-text-analysis scanning; CDC framing changes"
    alternatives: ["nonmedical health factors", "contributing factors to health outcomes", "living conditions affecting health"]
    notes: "Clinical SDOH use in specific care-delivery contexts (hospital discharge planning, care coordination) may survive; research-grant framing is RED."
    variants: ["SDOH", "social determinants"]

  # ---- RED additions (reproductive health) ----

  - term: "reproductive rights"
    severity: RED
    context: "Federal funding for abortion-related services restricted (Hyde Amendment + expansions); 'reproductive rights' as advocacy framing flagged"
    documented_action: "Statutory restrictions on federal funding for abortion; broad agency directives post-2025"
    alternatives: ["maternal health", "obstetric care", "women's clinical care (careful with 'women')"]
    variants: ["reproductive freedom", "reproductive justice"]

  - term: "reproductive justice"
    severity: RED
    context: "DEI + reproductive-rights intersection; both axes flagged"
    documented_action: "Same basis as 'reproductive rights'"
    alternatives: ["maternal health access", "community health services"]

  - term: "abortion"
    severity: RED
    context: "Federal funding statutorily restricted for most abortion services (Hyde); grant applications referencing abortion-related services risk ineligibility"
    documented_action: "Hyde Amendment (statutory); expanded restrictions under 2025 HHS directives"
    alternatives: ["carefully avoid in federal applications unless the program explicitly funds related services; prefer 'obstetric care', 'maternal health' in general framing"]
    variants: ["abortion care", "abortion access", "pregnancy termination"]

  # ---- YELLOW additions (climate / ESG scrutiny) ----

  - term: "sustainability"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI-era ESG framing; USDA 'sustainable agriculture' context-dependent (SARE program is statutory and valid)"
    documented_action: "Broadly scrutinized; SARE statutory programs unaffected"
    alternatives: ["long-term viability", "durable operations", "conservation (USDA context)"]
    notes: "SARE (Sustainable Agriculture Research and Education) is a statutory USDA program and remains valid. General 'sustainability' framing in other contexts is risky."
    variants: ["sustainable"]

  - term: "climate resilience"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Softer framing than 'climate change' but still flagged in some contexts"
    alternatives: ["weather preparedness", "storm preparedness", "drought adaptation", "farm operational resilience"]
    variants: ["climate adaptation"]

  - term: "global warming"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Synonymous with 'climate change' in administration scrutiny"
    alternatives: ["long-term temperature patterns", "weather variability"]

  - term: "impact investing"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "ESG-adjacent finance framing"
    alternatives: ["mission-aligned investment", "patient capital", "community investment"]

  - term: "stakeholder capitalism"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "ESG-adjacent governance framing"
    alternatives: ["shared-value business", "cooperative enterprise"]

  - term: "triple bottom line"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "ESG-adjacent framework"
    alternatives: ["financial + community + environmental metrics (decoupled framing)"]

  # ---- YELLOW additions (analytical DEI vocabulary) ----

  - term: "community-centered"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI framing signal"
    alternatives: ["community-driven", "community-owned", "member-led"]
    variants: ["community-centric"]

  - term: "culturally responsive"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Education/social-services DEI framing"
    alternatives: ["locally adapted", "community-informed", "place-based"]
    variants: ["culturally competent", "cultural responsiveness"]

  - term: "lived experience"
    severity: YELLOW
    progressive_register: PREFERRED  # activist/participatory-research/soul-fire funders actively welcome; centering lived experience is a value signal
    context: "DEI methodological framing"
    alternatives: ["direct experience", "first-hand experience", "participant perspective"]

  - term: "amplify"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI metaphor ('amplify voices')"
    alternatives: ["share", "feature", "present"]
    variants: ["amplify voices"]

  - term: "center"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI methodological framing ('center marginalized voices'); verb use only — 'community center' the noun is fine"
    alternatives: ["prioritize", "focus on", "feature"]
    variants: ["centering"]

  - term: "representation"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Political framing ('representation matters'); corporate-board representation is context-specific"
    alternatives: ["participation", "inclusion in (flagged)", "board composition (neutral)"]

  - term: "allyship"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI vocabulary"
    alternatives: ["partnership", "support", "collaboration"]
    variants: ["ally"]

  - term: "safe space"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI vocabulary (education/workplace)"
    alternatives: ["supportive environment", "respectful setting"]
    variants: ["safe spaces"]

  - term: "microaggressions"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI analytical vocabulary"
    alternatives: ["incivility", "disrespectful interactions"]
    variants: ["microaggression"]

  - term: "positionality"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI research methodology"
    alternatives: ["researcher perspective", "methodological context"]

  - term: "white privilege"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI analytical vocabulary; highly politicized"
    alternatives: ["historical advantage", "systemic access differences (flagged)"]
    variants: ["white supremacy (distinct but co-flagged)"]

  - term: "white supremacy"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Politicized term; academic and policy uses both risky"
    alternatives: ["documented historical exclusion", "racial hierarchy (also flagged)"]

  - term: "cisgender"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Linguistic marker for non-trans identity; flagged as gender-ideology-adjacent per EO 14168"
    alternatives: ["biological sex terminology per EO 14168 framing"]
    variants: ["cis"]

  - term: "patriarchy"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "DEI/feminist analytical framework"
    alternatives: ["historical gender norms (also risky)"]

  # ---- YELLOW additions (immigration) ----

  - term: "DACA"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Immigration relief program; politically charged"
    alternatives: ["eligible workforce (without status specification)"]
    variants: ["Dreamers", "Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals"]

  - term: "undocumented"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Immigration framing"
    alternatives: ["avoid status references in federal applications unless program explicitly serves a defined eligibility category"]
    variants: ["undocumented immigrants", "unauthorized"]

  - term: "sanctuary"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "'Sanctuary city', 'sanctuary campus' flagged; general 'sanctuary' (wildlife sanctuary) unflagged"
    alternatives: ["context matters — wildlife/conservation 'sanctuary' is fine; immigration-context 'sanctuary' is flagged"]
    variants: ["sanctuary city", "sanctuary campus", "sanctuary jurisdiction"]

  - term: "asylum seeker"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Immigration framing"
    alternatives: ["new arrivals", "eligible refugees (statutory — context-check)"]
    variants: ["asylum", "asylum-seeker"]

  # ---- YELLOW additions (health/clinical vocabulary) ----

  - term: "trauma-informed"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Clinical context (trauma-informed care) more tolerant; policy framing flagged"
    alternatives: ["patient-centered", "supportive care protocols"]
    variants: ["trauma informed", "trauma responsive"]

  - term: "social-emotional learning"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "State-level bans (FL, TX) + federal DEI scrutiny; education sector"
    alternatives: ["life-skills curriculum", "student development"]
    variants: ["SEL", "social emotional learning"]

  - term: "harm reduction"
    severity: YELLOW
    context: "Public-health intervention framing; drug-policy context flagged in some states/administrations"
    alternatives: ["overdose prevention", "clinical risk-reduction protocols"]

# =====================================================================
# Meta — operator approval block
# =====================================================================
#
# Operator review checklist:
# - [ ] Verify each RED entry has documented_action citing specific enforcement (EO, agency memo, funding pull)
# - [ ] Review YELLOW tier for entries that should escalate to RED based on your 2026 client experience
# - [ ] Add / remove / adjust severity per your admin-risk tolerance for each client org
# - [ ] Approve context/notes fields — especially the context-dependent entries (women, female, disabilities, underserved, minority, diversity, institutional)
# - [ ] Sign the approval_token field and move this file to admin_risk_register.yaml (supersedes v1)
# - [ ] Optionally: also move the file to the path POST step 6 expects (pipeline/institutional_memory/admin_risk_register.yaml), OR repoint POST step 6 to current path
#
# v2 DIFF SUMMARY:
#   - 17 → ~40 entries (+23)
#   - RED: 4 → 13 (+9)   — trans/LGBTQ+/gender family (8 entries), plus underrepresented, women, minority
#   - YELLOW: 7 → 19 (+12) — NSF leaked list coverage (marginalized, diversity, inclusion, CRT, woke,
#                             disparities, sense of belonging, institutional, activism, prejudice,
#                             privilege, disabilities, underserved, female, equal opportunity)
#   - GREEN: 6 → 7 (+1)  — no removals; intersectional kept GREEN pending documented pull
#
# v2.1 DIFF SUMMARY (expansion to cover ESG/climate/green + health equity + reproductive + immigration + analytical DEI):
#   - ~40 → ~75 entries (+~35)
#   - RED: 13 → ~29 (+~16)
#       Climate/ESG (11): climate change, green, ESG, renewable energy, clean energy, carbon,
#                          net-zero, decarbonization, greenhouse gas, just transition, environmental
#                          justice (cross-ref from v2)
#       Health (3): health equity, structural racism, social determinants of health
#       Reproductive (3): reproductive rights, reproductive justice, abortion
#   - YELLOW: 19 → ~38 (+~19)
#       Climate (5): sustainability, climate resilience, global warming, impact investing,
#                    stakeholder capitalism (+ triple bottom line)
#       Analytical DEI (14): community-centered, culturally responsive, lived experience, amplify,
#                             center, representation, allyship, safe space, microaggressions,
#                             positionality, white privilege, white supremacy, cisgender, patriarchy
#       Immigration (4): DACA, undocumented, sanctuary, asylum seeker
#       Clinical-DEI (3): trauma-informed, social-emotional learning, harm reduction
#   - GREEN: 7 → 7 (unchanged)
#
# KNOWN GAPS IN v2.1 (for operator consideration, not yet added):
#   - "progressive" (as political label — sometimes flagged, often fine)
#   - "advocacy" (context-dependent — community advocacy vs political advocacy)
#   - "oppression" / "liberation" (academic DEI framing)
#   - "settler-colonial" (decolonization-adjacent)
#   - "capitalism" / "anti-capitalism" (political framing)
#   - "environmental racism" (crosses env-justice + structural-racism axes; likely RED)
#   - "food apartheid" (activist framing for food deserts; progressive-register only)
#   - State-specific flagged lists (FL, TX, ID school-curriculum bans)
#   - Religious-liberty-context terms where applicants must thread a needle
#   - International-development terms ("capacity-building", "gender mainstreaming" etc.)
#
# SOURCES for v2.1 additions:
#   - Climate Action Campaign Trump Climate & Clean Energy Rollback Tracker
#   - Inside Climate News: $29B canceled/frozen climate+env grants (Sep 2025)
#   - NPR: DOE bans words including climate change and green (Sept 30, 2025)
#   - PBS NewsHour + CNBC: Oct 2025 $8B clean-energy cancellations
#   - PV Tech: US court rules DOE cancellation of $7.5B clean-energy grants unlawful
#   - Civil Eats + GovPing: USDA REAP rescinded April 2026
#   - Jones Day / Wilson Sonsini / Holland & Knight: EO legal analyses
#   - Notus: NIH pauses grants with 'health equity', 'structural racism' pending review
#   - CDC SDOH framing modifications tracking
#   - Hyde Amendment + 2025 HHS directives on reproductive health funding
